# (A `then` line waits for what the guest prints after the step before it:
# the statuses repeat, so a `serial` line would be satisfied by an earlier
# one and the next key could overtake its click, which is on another device.)
# Stage 7h's file manager (the approved mockups, docs/research/desktop/
# mockups/clear-field/files*.png): selection by click, Shift and Command,
# sorting by a header, the keyboard (arrows, Enter, Command+Up, Delete with
# its confirmation), search, rename in place, a new folder, a drag onto a
# folder that moves (Alt: copies), a double click, the context menu with
# Copy path and Open terminal here and its zosh lines in show-commands
# mode, the places. files tells the serial line its holds, every status
# line and every order. Coordinates are logical at scale 1: the file
# manager is the second window, its body at (105, 138); its rows at
# y = 232 + 28 n, its header at y 200, its toolbar at y 162.
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
type mkdir docs\r
screen ~> _
type echo a > a.txt\r
screen ~> _
type echo bb > b.txt\r
screen ~> _
type echo ccc > c.txt\r
screen ~> _
# The file manager from the dock, in home: the volume to read, ~ to change
# (INV-0168-2: the file service refused the volume to write).
click 427 723
then files: holds +r / +w ~
then files: ~ lists docs/ a.txt b.txt c.txt
pause 1500
# Focused by a click on its title bar (a new window does not take focus
# from the terminal).
click 545 119
pause 500
shot files-home
# A click, Shift to extend, Command to take one away.
click 409 260
then files: status 4 items · a.txt selected (2 B)
mclick shift 409 316
then files: status 4 items · 3 selected (9 B)
mclick meta 409 288
then files: status 4 items · 2 selected (6 B)
pause 300
shot files-select
# The size header: largest first, again smallest first; the name header.
click 805 200
then files: sorted by size down: docs c.txt b.txt a.txt
click 805 200
then files: sorted by size up: docs a.txt b.txt c.txt
click 349 200
then files: sorted by name up: docs a.txt b.txt c.txt
# The keyboard: arrows, Enter into a folder, Command+Up back out.
click 409 232
then files: status 4 items · docs selected (0 B)
key down
then files: status 4 items · a.txt selected (2 B)
key up
then files: status 4 items · docs selected (0 B)
key ret
then files: ~/docs lists
chord meta up
then files: ~ lists docs/ a.txt b.txt c.txt
# Search in the folder shown.
click 873 162
then files: keys go to the search
type b
then files: status 1 item matching “b”
key esc
then files: status 4 items
# Rename in place: F2, the stem replaced, Enter keeps it.
click 409 260
then files: status 4 items · a.txt selected (2 B)
key f2
then files: status Enter keeps the name · Escape leaves it
shot files-rename
type z
key ret
then files: Renamed a.txt to z.txt.
# Command+Shift+N: a new folder.
chord meta+shift n
then files: Made New folder.
# Delete asks first; Enter confirms. Rows: docs, New folder, b, c, z.
click 409 288
then files: status 5 items · b.txt selected (3 B)
key delete
then files: asks Delete b.txt?
pause 300
shot files-delete
key ret
then files: Deleted b.txt.
# A drag onto a folder moves; with Alt it copies. Rows: docs, New folder,
# c.txt, z.txt.
drag 409 288 409 232
then files: Moved c.txt to ~/docs.
mdrag alt 409 288 409 232
then files: Copied z.txt to ~/docs.
# A folder copied whole (Option onto docs).
mdrag alt 409 260 409 232
then files: Copied New folder to ~/docs.
# A double click enters the folder.
dclick 409 232
then files: ~/docs lists New folder/ c.txt z.txt
# The context menu on c.txt (the second row): Copy path.
rclick 409 260
then files: menu open
pause 300
shot files-menu
click 439 436
then files: Copied ~/docs/c.txt.
# In show-commands mode the menu writes each item's zosh line.
chord meta slash
rclick 409 260
then files: menu open
pause 300
shot files-menu-commands
key esc
then files: menu closed
chord meta slash
# Open terminal here: a terminal in this folder, in the window's room.
rclick 409 260
then files: menu open
pause 300
click 439 462
then files: A terminal in ~/docs.
pause 1500
# Up and back in the toolbar, and the place Home in the sidebar.
click 545 119
pause 300
click 201 162
then files: ~ lists docs/ New folder/ z.txt
click 131 162
then files: ~/docs lists
click 180 234
then files: ~ lists docs/ New folder/ z.txt
# A folder with everything in it deleted, after the card.
click 409 232
then files: status 3 items · docs selected (0 B)
key delete
then files: asks Delete docs?
key ret
then files: Deleted docs.
# The first terminal: power off.
click 85 400
pause 300
origin 73 106
type poweroff\r
exit
